      "notes": "All claims are well-grounded in cited evidence. Stated-tier claims quote verbatim from policy text accurately. Measurable claims (E25, E22, E13) are appropriately sourced and not overstated. The E22 source (visordown.com) is media/commercial but is used only to illustrate public sentiment, not as the sole basis for the direction verdict \u2014 acceptable. The projected claim (E31) is correctly tiered and the quote entails the claim. Tier integrity is sound: no projections presented as measurable facts. Magnitude/timing: 'moderate' and 'this-parliament' are defensible given the policy's broad but non-criminal scope. Direction 'improves' is well-supported under O10's defined scope (removal of state coercions over movement, consumer choice, mandates). No lever leakage \u2014 the verdict correctly defers health/safety effects to O5/O6. No party-blind issues; rationale is effect-based with no motive attribution. No false balance issue; 'improves' direction is consistent with the surviving claims. One minor observation: E22 (visordown.com) is a motorcycle media outlet citing a survey \u2014 the survey methodology is unverified \u2014 but it is used only as corroborating colour for public sentiment, not as structural support for the verdict, so this does not rise to blocking."
